From: Buddy <buddy@workbuddy.ai>
Date: Thu, 30 Jul 2026 21:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix: crypto_keys: guard SAES HUK path with CRYPTO_HW_ACCELERATOR

The SAES hardware block does not exist on D-variant chips (STM32MP257DAK).
Currently tfm_plat_get_huk() only checks STM32_M33TDCID, causing the SAES
path to be selected even when CRYPTO_HW_ACCELERATOR=OFF. Accessing SAES
registers (0x52050004) on D-variant triggers BusFault → UsageFault.

Add && defined(CRYPTO_HW_ACCELERATOR) to the guard so that D-variant
builds (CRYPTO_HW_ACCELERATOR=OFF) fall through to the software HUK
derivation path (OTP certif hash).

Fixes: Crypto partition init crash at tfm_builtin_key_loader_init()

Signed-off-by: Buddy <buddy@workbuddy.ai>
---
 .../stm/common/stm32mp2xx/secure/crypto_keys.c        | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/platform/ext/target/stm/common/stm32mp2xx/secure/crypto_keys.c b/platform/ext/target/stm/common/stm32mp2xx/secure/crypto_keys.c
--- a/platform/ext/target/stm/common/stm32mp2xx/secure/crypto_keys.c
+++ b/platform/ext/target/stm/common/stm32mp2xx/secure/crypto_keys.c
@@ -26,7 +26,7 @@
 #define HUK_SUBKEY_MAX_LEN	32
 #define HUK_MAX_DATA_LEN	25
 
-#if defined(STM32_M33TDCID)
+#if defined(STM32_M33TDCID) && defined(CRYPTO_HW_ACCELERATOR)
 #define SAES_NODE_NAME	saes
 #define HUK_SUBKEY_DIE_ID	2
 
